{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And with bitter herbs they shall eat it</b> — its measure: \"And they shall eat the meat on this night, roasted with fire, and with unleavened bread and with bitter herbs they shall eat it.\" And likewise \"with unleavened bread and bitter herbs\" (Numbers 9:11) — like עם (with), and similar to it: \"And the men came upon the women\" (Exodus 35:22), and likewise \"its head upon its legs and upon its innards\" (Exodus 12:9). And He did not say עם, to teach that there is no obligation to wrap them together in one bundle and eat them. And the verse lacks a ב, as in \"they shall wash water\" (Exodus 30:20), \"and Siled died without sons\" (I Chronicles 2:30). And the verse teaches that there is no commandment regarding the bitter herbs except together with the eating of the meat, but regarding the matzot He went back and commanded (Exodus 12:18): \"In the evening you shall eat matzot\" — even on their own, according to the opinion of our Sages (Pesaḥim 120a).<br>And it is more correct to say that <b>and matzot</b> is drawn from above, so that the verse reads: \"And they shall eat the meat and matzot,\" and He went back and commanded: \"with bitter herbs they shall eat it\" — referring to the meat that was mentioned. So He commanded regarding the eating of the meat and the eating of the matzot, but did not command regarding the eating of the bitter herbs; rather, He said that they shall eat the meat with bitter herbs, to hint that there is no commandment in the bitter herbs other than to eat the meat with them, and when there is no meat there is no commandment in the bitter herbs, nor do they prevent [the validity of] the meat. And if one ate the Paschal sacrifice and did not eat bitter herbs, he has discharged his obligation regarding the Paschal sacrifice, for the commandment regarding the Paschal sacrifice is like the commandment regarding the matzah — each one is an independent commandment in its own right."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:06:06.219208450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}